From fc57077e4bb8010ee143d85f5c6392645e85048d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Serhii Nikolaichuk <nikolaichuk.s.f@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 15:07:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] attest: the envelopes of the draft's CDDL on the wire;
 the reference implementation's media types

draft-novak-lamps-tacra-est (Envelope Definitions): "in the JSON encoding, bstr
members carry the unpadded base64url encoding of the octets". A Go []byte
encodes as padded standard base64, so a request from the reference
implementation (tacra-est, Python) was refused here, and ours would have been
refused there.

- The byte strings of the attested envelopes (handle, csr, cek_pub, evidence,
  endorsements; the Handle of attest-initiate) are B64URL. It writes
  unpadded base64url, and reads that or the padded standard base64 this
  package wrote before.
- attest-enroll and attest-retrieve also take the reference implementation's
  media types, application/est-attest-enroll+json and
  application/est-attest-retrieve+json, beside application/json. The draft
  asks IANA for media types and names none yet.

attest_ref_interop_test.go, on the reference implementation's messages from
a GCP SEV-SNP run (testdata/tacra-est-ref-vectors-sev-snp.json):
- each decodes with no unknown member and encodes back to the same JSON;
- sent with its media type, each reaches the attesting CA unchanged, and the
  Vault's container comes back as it was;
- the attest-initiate Handle goes out as unpadded base64url;
- padded standard base64 is still read.
The three tests fail on the code before this commit.
